  "id": "COMPOUND:6770 - PROTEIN:1477",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (9aS)-4-bromo-9a-butyl-7-hydroxy-1,2,9,9a-tetrahydro-3H-fluoren-3-one may interact with the Sodium- and chloride-dependent GABA transporter 1. This compound is linked to the Sodium channel subunit beta-2, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Npc11947 and (Z)-N-[(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-9-methyldec-7-enamide. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the GABA transporter, indicating a possible pathway through the Sodium channel subunit beta-2. The evidence also suggests that the compound may interact with potassium channel subfamily K member 3, which is a target of another compound that also affects the GABA transporter. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, the shared targets and the presence of a final link to the GABA transporter suggest a possible role in modulating the transporter through a common pathway involving ion channels. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for the compound to influence GABA transporter activity through ion channel regulation, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism.",
